SCYLLA Bot — Privacy Policy
Last Updated: 26 September 2026
This Privacy Policy explains how the SCYLLA Discord Bot ("SCYLLA", "the Bot", "we", "us", or "our") accesses, uses, stores, and protects information when you interact with the Bot.
SCYLLA is designed primarily for the SCYLLA Roblox Emergency Hospital community.
SCYLLA is an independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Discord Inc. or Roblox Corporation.
1. Information SCYLLA May Access
When you interact with SCYLLA, the Bot may access information provided through Discord's API, including:
- Discord user ID
- Discord username and display name
- Discord profile/avatar information
- Server ID
- Channel ID
- Discord roles
- Information you voluntarily submit through Bot commands
- Command and interaction information
Discord notes that bots can have access to baseline information such as usernames, avatars, nicknames and server roles. Discord Support
2. Information You Submit
Some SCYLLA features allow you to voluntarily provide information.
For example, this may include:
- Suggestions
- Player or staff reports
- Support ticket contents
- Roblox usernames
- Other information entered into SCYLLA commands
This information is used only to provide the requested Bot functionality and administer the SCYLLA community.
3. Roblox Information
When using features such as /roblox, SCYLLA may retrieve publicly available information from Roblox associated with the username provided.
This may include:
- Roblox username
- Display name
- Roblox user ID
- Avatar
- Account creation information
- Roblox group membership
- Group role/rank
SCYLLA does not request or store Roblox passwords.
4. How Information Is Used
Information accessed by SCYLLA may be used to:
- Process Bot commands
- Operate support tickets
- Process reports and suggestions
- Display Roblox profile information
- Determine Roblox group membership or rank
- Manage Discord permissions and Bot functionality
- Maintain security and prevent abuse
- Troubleshoot and improve the Bot
SCYLLA does not use Discord API data for advertising or sell Discord API data.
Discord's Developer Policy restricts developers from using API data outside the functionality necessary for their application and prohibits selling or disclosing it to advertising/data-broker services. Discord Support
5. Data Storage
SCYLLA may temporarily or persistently store information necessary to provide its features.
Information that no longer needs to be retained for the Bot's functionality may be deleted.
Messages created through features such as reports, suggestions and tickets may also remain within the SCYLLA Discord server until they are deleted by authorised server staff or through the relevant Bot functionality.
6. Sharing of Information
SCYLLA does not sell personal information.
Information may be visible to authorised SCYLLA staff where necessary to operate features such as reports, support tickets and server administration.
Information may also be processed through services required to operate the Bot, including Discord and Roblox.
Information may be disclosed where required by applicable law.
7. Data Security
Reasonable measures are taken to protect information processed or stored by SCYLLA from unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure or destruction.
However, no online service can guarantee absolute security.
8. Data Retention and Deletion
Information is retained only for as long as reasonably necessary to provide SCYLLA's functionality, resolve reports or support requests, maintain security, or comply with applicable requirements.
Discord's Developer Terms require developers to delete API data when retaining it is no longer necessary for the application's functionality or when an applicable user requests deletion, subject to applicable legal requirements. Discord Support
Users may request deletion of information associated with them by contacting the SCYLLA development team through the official SCYLLA Discord server.
Where applicable, the development team will identify and delete information associated with the requesting user.
9. Children's Privacy
SCYLLA is not intended to circumvent Discord's minimum-age requirements.
Users must meet Discord's applicable minimum-age requirements to use Discord and interact with SCYLLA.
10. Third-Party Services
SCYLLA relies on third-party services including:
Discord — provides the platform and Discord API used by the Bot.
Roblox — may provide publicly available Roblox account and group information used by Roblox-related commands.
Those services operate under their own privacy policies and terms.
11. Changes to This Privacy Policy
This Privacy Policy may be updated when SCYLLA's functionality or data-handling practices change.
The Last Updated date at the top of this document will indicate when the policy was most recently revised.
12. Contact
For privacy questions, data requests, or requests to delete information associated with you, contact the SCYLLA development team through the official SCYLLA Discord server.
